<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Artuqids of Mardin</h1><p class="st-meta">1106 CE – 1409 CE (approx.) · capital Mardin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The longest-lived branch of the Artuqid dynasty, ruling the hilltop city of Mardin for three centuries under Seljuk, Ayyubid and Mongol overlords.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilghazi">Ilghazi</a>, son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artuq-ibn-ekseb">Artuq</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a> in the early 12th century and made it the base of his branch of the family. In 1118 he also gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, and in 1119 he destroyed the army of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-antioch">Principality of Antioch</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ager-sanguinis">Field of Blood</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husam-al-din-timurtash">Timurtash</a> and later rulers held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a>, survived by accepting Zengid, Ayyubid and then Ilkhanid overlordship, and kept their dynasty intact through repeated invasions. Mardin, terraced on a steep hill, gained mosques and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a>, notably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Isa or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zinciriye-madrasa">Zinciriye Madrasa</a> of 1385. The region was home to many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syriac-christians">Syriac Christians</a>, including the patriarchal monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deyrulzafaran-monastery">Deyrulzafaran</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin's</a> lower city in 1394 and 1401. The last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artuqid-dynasty">Artuqids</a> were displaced by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qara-qoyunlu">Qara Qoyunlu</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> in 1409, and Mardin later passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1106 CE – 1409 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.71%;width:6.03%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1106 CE – 1409 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mardin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ilghazi, Timurtash, al-Zahir Isa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkic, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Artuqids of Mardin and Mayyafariqin, Artuqids</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1258&amp;focus=artuqids-of-mardin" aria-label="Artuqids of Mardin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5699 834 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Artuqids of Mardin lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6019 1090L5936 1127M6019 1090L6481 1127M6019 1090L5811 1337M6019 1090L6134 1224M6019 1090L6153 1065"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5936 1127h0M6481 1127h0M5811 1337h0M6134 1224h0M6153 1065h0